codes/llvm/libcxx/docs/DesignDocs/NoexceptPolicy.rst:2:``noexcept`` Policy
codes/llvm/libcxx/docs/DesignDocs/NoexceptPolicy.rst-3-===================
codes/llvm/libcxx/docs/DesignDocs/NoexceptPolicy.rst-4-
codes/llvm/libcxx/docs/DesignDocs/NoexceptPolicy.rst:5:Extended applications of ``noexcept``
codes/llvm/libcxx/docs/DesignDocs/NoexceptPolicy.rst-6--------------------------------------
codes/llvm/libcxx/docs/DesignDocs/NoexceptPolicy.rst-7-
codes/llvm/libcxx/docs/DesignDocs/NoexceptPolicy.rst-8-As of version 13 libc++ may mark functions that do not throw (i.e.,
codes/llvm/libcxx/docs/DesignDocs/NoexceptPolicy.rst:9:"Throws: Nothing") as ``noexcept``. This has two primary consequences:
codes/llvm/libcxx/docs/DesignDocs/NoexceptPolicy.rst-10-first, functions might not report precondition violations by throwing.
codes/llvm/libcxx/docs/DesignDocs/NoexceptPolicy.rst-11-Second, user-provided functions, such as custom predicates or custom
codes/llvm/libcxx/docs/DesignDocs/NoexceptPolicy.rst-12-traits, which throw might not be propagated up to the caller (unless
codes/llvm/libcxx/docs/DesignDocs/NoexceptPolicy.rst-13-specified otherwise by the Standard).
--
